      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "OS Command Injection in Ping Tool Endpoint: - Source: In `ping_host()`, user input is accepted via the JSON request body field `host` (`host = data.get('host', '')`).\n- Sanitization/Validation: The application only checks if `host` is non-empty (`if not host:`). No validation (such as regex matching for an IP/hostname) or sanitization/escaping of shell metacharacters is performed.\n- Sink: The unsanitized `host` is concatenated directly into a shell command formatted string `command = f\"ping -c 1 {host}\"` and executed via `os.system(command)`.\n- Conceptual Exploit Payload:\n  An attacker can send an HTTP POST request containing command chaining operators:\n  ```http\n  POST /api/tools/ping HTTP/1.1\n  Host: example.com\n  Content-Type: application/json\n\n  {\"host\": \"127.0.0.1; id\"}\n  ```\n  The server constructs and executes `ping -c 1 127.0.0.1; id`, which executes the `id` command with the privileges of the web application server."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 113,
                  "endLine": 114
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-78",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "OS Command Injection in Ping Tool Endpoint: - Source: In `ping_host()`, user input is accepted via the JSON request body field `host` (`host = data.get('host', '')`).\n- Sanitization/Validation: The application only checks if `host` is non-empty (`if not host:`). No validation (such as regex matching for an IP/hostname) or sanitization/escaping of shell metacharacters is performed.\n- Sink: The unsanitized `host` is concatenated directly into a shell command formatted string `command = f\"ping -c 1 {host}\"` and executed via `os.system(command)`.\n- Conceptual Exploit Payload:\n  An attacker can send an HTTP POST request containing command chaining operators:\n  ```http\n  POST /api/tools/ping HTTP/1.1\n  Host: example.com\n  Content-Type: application/json\n\n  {\"host\": \"127.0.0.1; id\"}\n  ```\n  The server constructs and executes `ping -c 1 127.0.0.1; id`, which executes the `id` command with the privileges of the web application server."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
