        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL Injection in User Search Endpoint: - Source: In `search_user()`, user input is read directly from the query parameter `username` via `username = request.args.get('username', '')`.\n- Sanitization/Validation: There is no input validation, escaping, or parameterized querying applied to `username`. It is directly interpolated into the SQL query string using an f-string.\n- Sink: `cursor.execute(query)` executes the raw string as an SQLite query.\n- Conceptual Exploit Payload:\n  An attacker can send the following GET request to extract user records bypassing intended query logic:\n  `GET /api/user/search?username='%20OR%20'1'='1 HTTP/1.1`\n  `Host: example.com`\n  This constructs `SELECT id, username, email, role FROM users WHERE username = '' OR '1'='1'`, returning all rows from the `users` table."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 70,
                  "endLine": 72
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-89",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL Injection in User Search Endpoint: - Source: In `search_user()`, user input is read directly from the query parameter `username` via `username = request.args.get('username', '')`.\n- Sanitization/Validation: There is no input validation, escaping, or parameterized querying applied to `username`. It is directly interpolated into the SQL query string using an f-string.\n- Sink: `cursor.execute(query)` executes the raw string as an SQLite query.\n- Conceptual Exploit Payload:\n  An attacker can send the following GET request to extract user records bypassing intended query logic:\n  `GET /api/user/search?username='%20OR%20'1'='1 HTTP/1.1`\n  `Host: example.com`\n  This constructs `SELECT id, username, email, role FROM users WHERE username = '' OR '1'='1'`, returning all rows from the `users` table."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
