            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639: Authorization Bypass Through User-Controlled Key",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) in Document Retrieval Endpoint: - Source: In `get_document(doc_id)`, the object identifier is passed via the URL path variable `doc_id`, and the requester's identity is passed via the `X-User-ID` HTTP header.\n- Sanitization/Validation: While the application checks that `X-User-ID` is provided (`if not current_user_id:`), it fails to verify that `current_user_id` matches the document's `owner_id` or that the user has authorization to view the requested document.\n- Sink: The database query `cursor.execute(\"SELECT id, owner_id, title, content FROM documents WHERE id = ?\", (doc_id,))` retrieves the record without access control restrictions, and returns it to the caller in `jsonify({\"status\": \"success\", \"data\": dict(doc)})`.\n- Conceptual Exploit Payload:\n  A non-privileged user authenticated with `X-User-ID: 2` (Alice) sends an HTTP request:\n  `GET /api/documents/1 HTTP/1.1`\n  `Host: example.com`\n  `X-User-ID: 2`\n  The server responds with HTTP 200 containing document 1 belonging to user 1 (`owner_id: 1`, \"Admin Confidential\", \"Super Secret Admin Report\")."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 92,
                  "endLine": 93
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) in Document Retrieval Endpoint: - Source: In `get_document(doc_id)`, the object identifier is passed via the URL path variable `doc_id`, and the requester's identity is passed via the `X-User-ID` HTTP header.\n- Sanitization/Validation: While the application checks that `X-User-ID` is provided (`if not current_user_id:`), it fails to verify that `current_user_id` matches the document's `owner_id` or that the user has authorization to view the requested document.\n- Sink: The database query `cursor.execute(\"SELECT id, owner_id, title, content FROM documents WHERE id = ?\", (doc_id,))` retrieves the record without access control restrictions, and returns it to the caller in `jsonify({\"status\": \"success\", \"data\": dict(doc)})`.\n- Conceptual Exploit Payload:\n  A non-privileged user authenticated with `X-User-ID: 2` (Alice) sends an HTTP request:\n  `GET /api/documents/1 HTTP/1.1`\n  `Host: example.com`\n  `X-User-ID: 2`\n  The server responds with HTTP 200 containing document 1 belonging to user 1 (`owner_id: 1`, \"Admin Confidential\", \"Super Secret Admin Report\")."
          },
